#
#==================================================================================================
#
# OSCAR (Orbital Spacecraft Active Removal) Input File
# [v2.4.4, 07/2024]
#
#==================================================================================================
#
# 1) Basic Settings
#
#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Begin Date: Date the simulation starts at in YYYY MM DD hh mm ss format
#
  2016 11 01 12 00 00 ! [YYYY MM DD hh mm ss]
#
# Run-ID (max. 25 characters, no spaces) 
#
  oscar 
#
# Comment lines (two lines, 80 characters each)
#
  DRAMA
  OSCAR - Orbital Spacecraft Active Removal
#
# Target Orbit
#
  6900.0    semi-major axis / km
  0.000100    eccentricity / -
  98.6    inclination / deg
  60.00    right ascension of ascending node (RAAN) / deg
  80.00    argument of perigee / deg
  180.00    mean anomaly / deg
#
# Spacecraft Parameters
#
  10.000    cross-sectional area / m**2
  2500.0    spacecraft dry mass / kg (can be either dry or total mass - specified by following switch)
  1         dry mass switch (1 = dry mass, 0 = wet mass, i.e. dry mass + propellant mass)
  2.2       drag coefficient
  1.3       reflectivity coefficient
#
#==================================================================================================
#
# 2) Disposal/Removal Options
#
#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Disposal Option
#
# 1 = Direct De-Orbit
# 2 = Delayed De-Orbit
# 3 = Re-Orbit
# 4 = none
#
  4 
#
# Disposal System
#
# 1 = Chemical Propulsion System
# 2 = Electric Propulsion System
# 3 = Electrodynamic Tether System
# 4 = Drag Augmentation Device
#
  1 
#
# Scenario Options:
#
#
  1    Number of Hohmann Maneuvers (only chemical propulsion system)
   60.0    Perigee altitude for direct de-orbit / km 
  2000.0    Re-Orbit Altitude / km (only "Re-Orbit" disposal option) 
  25.0    Lifetime Limit / years (only "Delayed De-Orbit" disposal option) 
  5.0    Lifetime Margin / percent (mandated conservative margin of error for OSCAR: 5.0% according to ISO-27852:2011) 
#
# Chemical Propulsion
#
  Cold Gas
  60.0    Specific Impulse / s
#
# Electric Propulsion
#
  Ion 1 (T5)
  3248.0          Specific Impulse / s
     18.000000    Total Thrust / mN
  100000.0         Thruster Lifetime / h
#
# Electrodynamic Tether
#
  5.0    Tether Length / km
  275.0    Tether Resistance / Ohm
  35.26    Tether Relative Angle / deg
#
# Drag Augmentation
#
  10.0    Cross-Sectional Area / m**2
  2.2    Drag Coefficient
  1.3    Solar Reflectivity Coefficient
#
#==================================================================================================
#
# 3) Orbit Prediction
#
#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Propagation span / years
#
  100.0
#
# Solar & Geomagnetic Activity Scenario
#
# 1 = Latest Prediction
# 2 = Best Case / Worst Case (+ Confidence Interval)
# 3 = Constant Solar Flux    (+ Value OR automatically computed)
# 4 = ECSS Sample Solar Cycle
# 5 = Monte Carlo Sampling   (+ No. of Sampled Cycles)
#
  1
#
#--------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Latest Prediction Scenario options
#  
  1    Solar & Geomagnetic Activity data to be used (1 = ESA, 2 = User-defined)
#
#--------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Best Case / Worst Case scenario options
#
  50.0 
#
#--------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Constant Solar Flux scenario options
#
  2    Mode Switch (1 = auto, i.e. value computed from ballistic parameter an object's orbit; 2 = user-defined)
  200.0    User-defined constant solar flux level / (10**(-22) W/m**2/Hz)
  15.0     User-defined constant geomagnetic activity Ap
#
#--------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Monte Carlo Sampling scenario options
#
  5    No. of sampled cycles [1:6]
#
#==================================================================================================
#
# 4) Plot Options
#
#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Generate Plots
#
# 1 = yes
# 0 = no
#
  1    Altitude vs. Time
  1    Eccentricity vs. Time
  0    Inclination vs. RAAN (geosynchronous region)
  1    Inclination vs. Time
  0    Altitude vs. Declination (geosynchronous region)
  1    Solar and geomagnetic activity vs. Time
  0     -- not implemented --
#
# Linestyle of Data in Plot
#
   1
#
# Plot Critical Altitude
#
# 1 = yes
# 0 = no
#
  0
#
# Linestyle of Critical Altitude
#
  3
#
#==================================================================================================
